[Unit]
Description=Scheduled restart of option-decode-worker (Prisma native query engine RSS mitigation)
# Prisma's native query engine (library engine, loaded in-process) has a
# known, currently-unresolved upstream memory leak - RSS grows steadily
# with general query activity and is never released back to the OS, while
# process.memoryUsage() stays flat throughout (see
# https://github.com/prisma/prisma/issues/25371 and similar reports across
# Prisma 5.x-6.x, multiple DBs, multiple query shapes - not specific to any
# query pattern in this codebase). Confirmed in production (2026-07-31):
# worker RSS reached 5.6-5.9GB within 15min-1.5hrs of a fresh restart on a
# freshly-resized 7.6GB host, refilling swap. Two app-level attempts to fix
# this by bounding Prisma createMany() SQL-shape cardinality
# (packages/db/src/market-repository.ts, wave-price-repository.ts, commits
# dfac908/5cc1700) did not stop the growth - the leak tracks general query
# volume, not any specific call site's shape.
#
# Until Prisma fixes this upstream (or this app migrates to Prisma's
# driver-adapters mode, bypassing the native engine entirely - a separate,
# properly-tested project), the practical mitigation is to recycle the
# worker process periodically, well before RSS approaches the host's
# memory ceiling. BullMQ's repeatable/scheduled jobs resume automatically
# on the next tick after a restart - no data loss, same behavior already
# exercised multiple times manually today with no ill effects.
After=option-decode-worker.service

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/usr/bin/systemctl restart option-decode-worker.service
